## Access Control

This project uses Supabase Auth instead of a custom Express/JWT/bcrypt implementation.

Supabase handles:
- Password hashing and salting
- User registration
- Login authentication
- JWT/session generation
- Token validation

The frontend stores the Supabase session using the Supabase client. Protected data access depends on the authenticated user session. Database-level access control is enforced using Supabase Row Level Security policies.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Frontend as React Frontend
    participant Auth as Supabase Auth
    participant DB as Supabase Database

    User->>Frontend: Enter email/password on sign-up form
    Frontend->>Auth: supabase.auth.signUp(credentials)
    Auth->>DB: Create auth user
    Auth-->>Frontend: Return session/JWT or confirmation response
    Frontend-->>User: Show signed-in state or confirmation message
```

